{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אמונה עד בא השמש", :translit "emunah ad ba ha-shemesh", :gloss "faith until the sun comes"} {:he "אמונה", :translit "emunah", :gloss "faith"} {:he "והאמין בה'", :translit "ve-he'emin ba-shem", :gloss "and he believed in YHWH"} {:he "עד בא", :translit "ad ba", :gloss "until comes"} {:he "ויצחק בא מבא", :translit "ve-yitzchak ba mi-vo", :gloss "and Isaac came from coming"} {:he "השמש", :translit "ha-shemesh", :gloss "the sun"} {:he "וילן שם כי בא השמש", :translit "va-yalan sham ki ba ha-shemesh", :gloss "and he lodged there, for the sun had come"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Three consecutive phrases from Moses's hands being steadfast mapped one-to-one to the three Patriarchs by verbal linkage to Genesis verses"}], :frame {:text "The phrase describing Moses's hands as steadfast (Exodus 17:12) is read as an allusion to the merit of the three Patriarchs. Abraham is the archetype of faith through Genesis 15:6, 'and he believed in YHWH.' Isaac is identified by the verbal root בוא in Genesis 26:32, 'and Isaac came.' Jacob is identified by the phrase 'the sun came' in Genesis 28:11, 'and he lodged there, for the sun had set' — here rendered 'for the sun had come,' matching the Exodus wording.", :sources ["Exodus 17:12" "Genesis 15:6" "Genesis 26:32" "Genesis 28:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Three consecutive phrases from Moses's hands being steadfast mapped one-to-one to the three Patriarchs by verbal linkage to Genesis verses", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:16:53.923440271Z", :model "glm-5.2"}